## Interactive Playwright testing (click-through flows)

Playwright is not limited to screenshots — it can click, type, navigate, and interact with any element. Use this when you need to verify behavior beyond static appearance (e.g. tap a button and confirm a sheet appears, fill a form field, test navigation transitions).

### Available APIs

```js
// Click any element
await page.click('#myButton');
await page.locator('text=Submit').click();
await page.locator('.job-card').first().click();

// Type into fields
await page.fill('#ct-type-input', 'AC unit not cooling');
await page.locator('select').selectOption({ label: 'DAN DAY' });

// Wait for things to appear
await page.waitForSelector('.bottom-sheet', { timeout: 5000 });
await page.waitForTimeout(1000); // simple delay (ms)

// Assert element is visible
const visible = await page.locator('#myModal').isVisible().catch(() => false);

// Run JS in the browser context
await page.evaluate(() => window.switchScreen('workspace'));

// Take a screenshot at any point
await page.screenshot({ path: '_ss_step1.png' });
```

### Pattern: write a targeted interaction script

When testing a specific flow, write a custom `.mjs` script (don't modify the standard `_check_screenshot.mjs`):

```js
// _test_flow.mjs — one-off test, delete after reviewing
import { chromium } from 'playwright';
const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true });
const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 390, height: 844 }, deviceScaleFactor: 2 });
const page = await ctx.newPage();
await page.goto('https://vertex-core-db.web.app/technician/index.html?vc_debug=0', { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 15000 });
await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
await page.locator('select').first().selectOption({ label: 'DAN DAY' });
await page.waitForTimeout(500);
await page.locator('#loginContinueBtn').click({ timeout: 5000 });
await page.waitForTimeout(4000);

// --- custom interaction steps go here ---
await page.locator('.job-card').first().click();
await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
await page.screenshot({ path: '_ss_workspace.png' });

await page.locator('#navMenuBtn').click();
await page.waitForTimeout(500);
await page.screenshot({ path: '_ss_menu_open.png' });
// ----------------------------------------

await browser.close();
```

Run with: `node _test_flow.mjs`

### SDK slices: `playwrightSteps`

SDK slices that set `uiChange: true` can also provide a `playwrightSteps` array on the `Slice` definition. These are raw JS lines injected into the generated Playwright script **after login and before the final screenshot**, allowing the runner to test a specific flow automatically:

```ts
uiChange: true,
playwrightSteps: [
  `await page.locator('.job-card').first().click();`,
  `await page.waitForTimeout(3000);`,
  `await page.waitForSelector('#navMenuBtn', { timeout: 5000 });`,
],
```

The build runner injects these steps between login and the workspace screenshot, then sends the result to the cheap model (`gpt-5.4-mini`) for visual comparison as usual.

### Cleanup

Always delete temporary test `.mjs` scripts and `.png` files after reviewing. Do not commit them.

